    D --> E{High System Load?};
    E -- Yes --> F[Lower Maximum Processor Usage];
    E -- No --> G[Read System Error Log];
    G --> H{Errors Found?};
    H -- Yes --> I[Address Errors];
    H -- No --> J[Increase Fan Speed];
    I --> J;
    J --> K[Monitor Temperature];
    K --> L{Temperature Stable?};
    L -- Yes --> Z;
    L -- No --> M[Decrease Room Temperature];
    M --> K;
    Z[End: Monitor Temperature];
```

**Explanation of Flow Diagram:**

The flow diagram outlines a systematic approach to identifying and addressing the temperature issue. It starts by observing the temperature trend. If an increasing trend is detected, the system reads the current temperature and system load. Based on the load, it either lowers processor usage or checks for errors. If no errors are found, the fan speed is increased. The process continues to monitor the temperature until it stabilizes. If errors are found, they are addressed, and the temperature is monitored. The diagram provides a clear path for intervention based on the observed data.


